---
import './design-aids.css';
---
<design-json-value id="json-value-lab" class="lab design-aid design-lab" aria-labelledby="json-value-title">
  <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span></div>
  <h3 id="json-value-title">What is stored at capacity_ml?</h3>
  <div class="lab-introduction">
    <p>P7’s optional product details live in <code>attributes jsonb</code>. Compare a capacity, a missing field and JSON null. This diagnostic probe also permits SQL NULL for the whole column; an <code>attributes NOT NULL</code> rule would reject that case.</p>
    <p class="try-this">Change the stored value. Compare extracting JSON with <code>-&gt;</code>, extracting text with <code>-&gt;&gt;</code>, and checking the JSON type. In the result, SQL NULL means there is no SQL value; the word <code>null</code> is a JSON value.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-controls" data-controls>
    <p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
    <div class="control-line"><label for="json-stored-value">Stored attributes</label><select id="json-stored-value" data-value><option value="number">JSON number: 350</option><option value="string">JSON string: "350"</option><option value="missing">Key missing: {'{}'}</option><option value="json-null">JSON null: {'{"capacity_ml": null}'}</option><option value="sql-null">Whole column: SQL NULL</option></select></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-output paper-surface">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Result <span>PostgreSQL expressions on this one value</span></p>
    <div class="design-record"><h4>P7 · stored attributes</h4><p class="design-sql" data-stored>{'{"capacity_ml": 350}'}</p></div>
    <div class="design-expression"><code>attributes ? 'capacity_ml'</code><strong data-present>TRUE</strong></div>
    <div class="design-expression"><code>attributes -&gt; 'capacity_ml'</code><strong data-json>350</strong></div>
    <div class="design-expression"><code>attributes -&gt;&gt; 'capacity_ml'</code><strong data-text>350 (text)</strong></div>
    <div class="design-expression"><code>jsonb_typeof(attributes -&gt; 'capacity_ml')</code><strong data-type>number</strong></div>
    <p class="design-state" data-message role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">The JSON number is 350. Extracting text also produces 350, but that text no longer tells us the JSON type.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="model-note"><summary>What this model leaves out</summary><p>These are fixed examples of PostgreSQL jsonb operators, not a database connection. The key-existence operator here tests a top-level key. The model does not cast the extracted text to a number or impose a capacity rule. SQL NULL also propagates through the existence test: it is UNKNOWN, rather than FALSE.</p></details>
  <noscript><p>The number 350 and string "350" both extract as the text 350. Their JSON types differ. A missing key and JSON null both extract as SQL NULL with <code>-&gt;&gt;</code>; <code>-&gt;</code> and jsonb_typeof distinguish them. If the whole column is SQL NULL, all four expressions produce SQL NULL.</p></noscript>
</design-json-value>
<script>
  class DesignJsonValue extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      const value = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-value]')!;
      const examples: Record<string, { stored:string; present:string; json:string; text:string; type:string; message:string }> = {
        number: { stored:'{"capacity_ml": 350}', present:'TRUE', json:'350', text:'350 (text)', type:'number', message:'The JSON number is 350. Extracting text also produces 350, but that text no longer tells us the JSON type.' },
        string: { stored:'{"capacity_ml": "350"}', present:'TRUE', json:'"350"', text:'350 (text)', type:'string', message:'The JSON string is "350". Text extraction gives the same 350 as the numeric case; jsonb_typeof reveals that the stored value is a string.' },
        missing: { stored:'{}', present:'FALSE', json:'SQL NULL', text:'SQL NULL', type:'SQL NULL', message:'capacity_ml is absent. Both extraction operators produce SQL NULL. The existence test is FALSE: there is no key.' },
        'json-null': { stored:'{"capacity_ml": null}', present:'TRUE', json:'null (JSON)', text:'SQL NULL', type:'null (text)', message:'capacity_ml exists and holds JSON null. JSON extraction preserves it; text extraction produces SQL NULL. The type function returns the text null.' },
        'sql-null': { stored:'SQL NULL', present:'SQL NULL', json:'SQL NULL', text:'SQL NULL', type:'SQL NULL', message:'The whole SQL column has no value. Every expression produces SQL NULL, including the existence test; its truth value is UNKNOWN.' },
      };
      const render = () => {
        const example = examples[value.value];
        for (const key of ['stored','present','json','text','type','message'] as const) this.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`)!.textContent = example[key];
      };
      value.addEventListener('change', render);
      render(); this.dataset.ready = 'true';
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('design-json-value')) customElements.define('design-json-value', DesignJsonValue);
</script>
